import{_ as i,o as a,c as n,a2 as s}from"./chunks/framework.CDpkVv68.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Tinkering","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/game-design/professions/tinkering.md","filePath":"en/game-design/professions/tinkering.md"}'),t={name:"en/game-design/professions/tinkering.md"};function o(r,e,l,c,d,p){return a(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="tinkering" tabindex="-1">Tinkering <a class="header-anchor" href="#tinkering" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Tinkering&quot;">​</a></h1><p><strong>Design status:</strong> Proposed; all mechanics, examples and technique paths below remain candidates. <strong>Implementation:</strong> no implementation of this redesign is established by this documentation batch. <strong>Availability:</strong> not established. <strong>Verification:</strong> documentation review only; no gameplay test. <strong>Reviewed:</strong> 2026-10-09 for public projection; design status and mechanics preserved from the canonical specification.</p><p><a href="/Syrolands-Public/en/guide/professions/tinkering.html">Player-facing overview</a> · <a href="/Syrolands-Public/en/game-design/professions/profession-system.html">Profession System</a></p><h2 id="purpose-and-profession-loop" tabindex="-1">Purpose and profession loop <a class="header-anchor" href="#purpose-and-profession-loop" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Purpose and profession loop&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Tinkering is precision mechanics / engineering / mechanisms.</p><h3 id="core-loop" tabindex="-1">Core loop <a class="header-anchor" href="#core-loop" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Core loop&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Inspect -&gt; Design -&gt; Assemble -&gt; Calibrate -&gt; Test -&gt; Maintain</p><p>Identity: Tinkering is a deliberately &quot;nerdy&quot; profession that supports many specialized gameplay families.</p><h3 id="abstract-mechanism-model" tabindex="-1">Abstract mechanism model <a class="header-anchor" href="#abstract-mechanism-model" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Abstract mechanism model&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Power</li><li>Motion</li><li>Trigger</li><li>Control</li><li>Output</li></ul><h3 id="possible-component-logic-families" tabindex="-1">Possible component/logic families <a class="header-anchor" href="#possible-component-logic-families" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Possible component/logic families&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Inputs/triggers:</p><ul><li>switch;</li><li>pressure plate;</li><li>tripwire;</li><li>timer;</li><li>contact;</li><li>other mechanical triggers.</li></ul><p>Logic/control:</p><ul><li>simple AND/OR/NOT-like behavior;</li><li>delays;</li><li>counters;</li><li>relays;</li></ul><p>but keep it intentionally bounded.</p><p>Outputs:</p><ul><li>doors;</li><li>gates;</li><li>cages;</li><li>bells;</li><li>feeders;</li><li>pulleys;</li><li>traps;</li><li>lights;</li><li>dispensers;</li><li>other mechanisms.</li></ul><h3 id="housing-automation" tabindex="-1">Housing automation <a class="header-anchor" href="#housing-automation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Housing automation&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Tinkering should eventually allow players to create mechanical logic systems inside housing, conceptually similar to a constrained redstone/logic-gate layer:</p><ul><li>switch opens gate;</li><li>timer activates feeder;</li><li>motion/pressure trigger activates alarm;</li><li>mechanical sequence operates cage/pulley;</li></ul><p>etc.</p><p>Housing automation is a future proposal, outside implementation scope.</p><h3 id="locks-security" tabindex="-1">Locks/security <a class="header-anchor" href="#locks-security" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Locks/security&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Tinkering can create and inspect locks/mechanical security. Lockpicking defeats them. Tinkering + Lockpicking provides richer understanding.</p><p>Housing should not necessarily be magically impenetrable. Future burglary gameplay may include:</p><ul><li>inspecting locks;</li><li>lockpicking outer doors;</li><li>hidden/stealth movement;</li><li>Detect Hidden for traps/alarms;</li><li>Remove Trap/Tinkering for countermeasures;</li><li>locked internal containers;</li><li>alarm countdowns;</li><li>guard/security response;</li><li>risk escalation.</li></ul><p>Balance must prevent trivial AFK lockpicking/total house loss.</p><h3 id="traps" tabindex="-1">Traps <a class="header-anchor" href="#traps" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Traps&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Modular combination of trigger + mechanism + output/payload. Alchemy can provide payloads. Tinkering provides control/delivery.</p><h3 id="reverse-engineering" tabindex="-1">Reverse engineering <a class="header-anchor" href="#reverse-engineering" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Reverse engineering&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>inspect;</li><li>disassemble;</li><li>infer mechanism;</li><li>reconstruct;</li><li>risk damage;</li><li>discover techniques from world devices.</li></ul><h3 id="dungeon-utility" tabindex="-1">Dungeon utility <a class="header-anchor" href="#dungeon-utility" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Dungeon utility&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>repair mechanisms;</li><li>restore lifts/bridges;</li><li>bypass mechanical systems;</li><li>diagnose traps;</li><li>operate machinery.</li></ul><h3 id="golems-mechanical-automatons" tabindex="-1">Golems / mechanical automatons <a class="header-anchor" href="#golems-mechanical-automatons" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Golems / mechanical automatons&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Tinkering should eventually support high-end mechanical constructs.</p><p>Possible progression:</p><ul><li>simple toys/devices;</li><li>utility automatons;</li><li>pack/maintenance constructs;</li><li>stationary mechanisms;</li><li>combat-capable constructs;</li><li>true mechanical golems as high-end specialization.</li></ul><p>Large constructs may require collaboration:</p><ul><li>Blacksmithing for frame/armor;</li><li>Tinkering for movement/control;</li><li>Alchemy for power/lubricants/volatile systems;</li><li>possibly Inscription/Magery for magical control/binding, if later accepted.</li></ul><p>Golems remain a future high-end specialization direction; detailed design is deferred.</p><h2 id="knowledge-and-specialization" tabindex="-1">Knowledge and specialization <a class="header-anchor" href="#knowledge-and-specialization" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Knowledge and specialization&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Mechanist&#39;s Journal.</strong> World devices can teach techniques through inspection and risky reverse engineering. Precision mechanics, security and future constructs provide distinct specialist identities.</p><h2 id="shared-progression-production-and-economy" tabindex="-1">Shared progression, production and economy <a class="header-anchor" href="#shared-progression-production-and-economy" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Shared progression, production and economy&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <a href="/Syrolands-Public/en/game-design/characters/skills-and-skillcap.html">character skill framework</a> owns teaching and cap/gain direction. The <a href="/Syrolands-Public/en/game-design/professions/profession-system.html">Profession System</a> owns craft discovery, knowledge sharing, manual mastery, batch production, commissions and multidimensional reputation. Those rules are not independently redefined here. The <a href="/Syrolands-Public/en/game-design/items/itemization-and-craft-quality.html">quality specification</a> owns the shared result envelope and rare item properties.</p><h2 id="related-skills-and-field-interactions" tabindex="-1">Related skills and field interactions <a class="header-anchor" href="#related-skills-and-field-interactions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related skills and field interactions&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Lockpicking defeats locks while Tinkering understands/builds them; together they provide richer understanding. Detect Hidden and Remove Trap may support burglary counterplay. Alchemy supplies payload/power/lubricant candidates; Blacksmithing supplies frames, Carpentry structures, and future Magery/Inscription may provide control only if accepted.</p><p><a href="/Syrolands-Public/en/game-design/professions/alchemy.html">Alchemy</a> · <a href="/Syrolands-Public/en/game-design/professions/blacksmithing.html">Blacksmithing</a> · <a href="/Syrolands-Public/en/game-design/professions/carpentry.html">Carpentry</a> · <a href="/Syrolands-Public/en/game-design/magic.html">Magery and Inscription</a> · <a href="/Syrolands-Public/en/game-design/living-world.html#protection-and-regeneration">Protection and regeneration</a>.</p><h2 id="abstraction-and-technical-boundary" tabindex="-1">Abstraction and technical boundary <a class="header-anchor" href="#abstraction-and-technical-boundary" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Abstraction and technical boundary&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Keep only state and feedback that support meaningful decisions. The <a href="/Syrolands-Public/en/game-design/professions/profession-system.html#performance-abstraction-and-authority">shared abstraction/authority constraints</a> and living-world architecture apply; persistence requires a separate technical design. Nothing here selects packet IDs, schemas, timers, UI assets or runtime algorithms.</p><h2 id="open-questions" tabindex="-1">Open questions <a class="header-anchor" href="#open-questions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Open questions&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Limits on logic chains, timers and active mechanisms; housing permissions and burglary losses; traps, detection, alarms and counterplay; reverse-engineering loss and knowledge; construct control, costs and persistence. Golems remain a high-end direction without recipes, stats, AI or a chosen magical binding system.</p><p>The <a href="/Syrolands-Public/en/game-design/professions/profession-system.html#open-questions-and-reconciliation-required">shared reconciliation register</a> owns cross-system conflicts. Existing combat experiments and evidence do not validate this profession redesign.</p><h2 id="proposed-training-facilities-—-batch-05" tabindex="-1">Proposed training facilities — Batch 05 <a class="header-anchor" href="#proposed-training-facilities-—-batch-05" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Proposed training facilities — Batch 05&quot;">​</a></h2><p><a href="/Syrolands-Public/en/game-design/characters/familiarity.html#training-facilities-and-crafts">Shared Familiarity and facilities</a> considers crafted dummies, articulated/moving targets, range mechanisms and magical practice foci, with Carpentry, Tinkering and Inscription as possible contributors. Roles/recipes are not allocated here. Facilities should efficiently maintain fluency, not become optimal core-skill grinding or bypass discovery.</p>',55)])])}const u=i(t,[["render",o]]);export{m as __pageData,u as default};
